<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:46:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military base in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cd1ceede5b61ffc9bba5c37e3081ee0941ed25298fe3acbb7a88bc65e1a0e43</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:44:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:29:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain--f851a46df3dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain" /><summary type="html">Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September as blasts rocked the capital, Manama. It comes after Iran targeted an airbase in the US-allied island state, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East War and comes as negotiations to end the conflict remain at a stalemate, with the US maintaining its naval blockade and Iran its stranglehold over the strait of Hormuz. Story by Rachael Griffiths.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canaries urge government action after 2,200 migrants reach the islands in 48h</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb4e0c8b64bed15bcb26111d2956f105869e94712fb2fce4f025635ff94ac9ee</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:24:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1--7c412d3109df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1" /><summary type="html">Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The Spanish islands are one of the main entry points into Europe for migrants from Africa. The Spanish Interior Ministry says more than 13,000 arrived there between January and the end of last month. Details and analysis by Andrew Hilliar, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: The French Connection</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94bd1a08cc298e565c0539682b898a477d64951ed7387678d19fcfd61ad3bb93</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:03:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection--c681b71603cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection" /><summary type="html">President Trump is heading to Asia in a few days time, and will meet President Putin and President Xi. There's likely to be one fewer tech giants at the table, Jensen Huang, newly resigned from Nvidia, over the suspected spy affair.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Santa school in full swing in London ahead of Christmas celebrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b9a78c159ab5b0817e5eb303a57ff124e83876bded3a7951d5b86041a10ef77</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:35:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/santa-school-in-full-swing-in-london-ahead-of-christmas-celebrations--5731bcbd3ec7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/santa-school-in-full-swing-in-london-ahead-of-christmas-celebrations" /><summary type="html">It may still be November but it's beginning to look a lot like Christmas in South London, as many Santa impersonators are heading to school for their festive training. The school, organised by an event company called Ministry of Fun, brings together Santas, elves, and Mrs Clauses to share experiences, practice belly laughs and learn how to bring the magic of Christmas to life. Story by Rachael Griffiths.</summary></entry><entry><title>A deep dive into Ivory Coast's solar energy goals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65736d51c58b2de5bafbec6151b9eca31903415145595f43cc3f65603f5b9d82</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:25:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-deep-dive-into-ivory-coast-s-solar-energy-goals--daefc9aa7c4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-deep-dive-into-ivory-coast-s-solar-energy-goals" /><summary type="html">Can Ivory Coast, which remains heavily dependent on fossil fuels, turn to solar power to make its energy consumption greener and more sustainable? We visited the country's new solar power plant in Ferkessédougou, in the north of the country. Inaugurated in July, it is expected to generate nearly 90 gigawatt-hours of electricity a year. Report by Julia Guggenheim.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why the Nvidia scandal is bad news for Europe’s AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b61857e6e61a1a503fa686549965f140dbc018a0a65e4671120713984261ccd6</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:16:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261115-why-the-nvidia-scandal-is-bad-news-for-europe-s-ai-ambitions--6d8047c5fc4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261115-why-the-nvidia-scandal-is-bad-news-for-europe-s-ai-ambitions" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's Jensen Huang poured money into open-source AI, from French-founded Hugging Face to chips for Mistral's data centres, and fought Washington's attempts to restrict it. With Huang gone and China hawks emboldened, Tech 24 asks whether Europe's AI ambitions have lost their most powerful ally, and whether he was ever the champion Europe needed.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>US probes nationwide flights stoppage as travel disruptions persist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74ba8a90d1ceb8d0254f84c4857a4bdb4c1fe23ad721d049949203e0a2939414</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:09:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist--66080e063e19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist" /><summary type="html">US air travel is expected to return to normal this Sunday, following a nationwide ground stop Friday night that stranded hundreds of thousands of passengers and disrupted travel worldwide. The Trump administration blamed the incident on a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines and said there was no evidence this was a cyberattack. The ground stop now raises questions about the country's aging infrastructure and lawmakers are calling for an investigation. Analysis by Philip Mann, aviation expert at Vector Strategic Consulting.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chinese spy, chip sales, Trump ties... The Nvidia scandal deepens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9bfc5b0cd9d55ce73c161b67678075e44dfaade9df200c98bf4f6869219ffa7</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:00:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/chinese-spy-chip-sales-trump-ties-the-nvidia-scandal-deepens--f307af3a264f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-spy-chip-sales-trump-ties-the-nvidia-scandal-deepens" /><summary type="html">The Nvidia scandal continues to unravel. Sunday, the Singapore-based company Megaspeed said that Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang had officially left the company in 2025. She is the alleged Chinese spy that had an affair with Nvidia's former CEO Jensen Huang. Late last year, revelations showed she was being investigated for chip smuggling. The scandal has also raised questions about how much the US government knew – Trump was allegedly warned about the affair but did not react. Analysis by Laïla Mörch, CEO of Shael and tech investor in Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Spain protests, Pope Leo's Peru 'homecoming' and Rocky fans in Philly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c775b29f56dd81f3e339df322af472e521391a134ede9adce869ba2938ba4862</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:59:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-the-week-in-pictures-spain-protests-pope-leo-peru-homecoming-rocky-fans-philly-rosalia--e99d0a43c1b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-the-week-in-pictures-spain-protests-pope-leo-peru-homecoming-rocky-fans-philly-rosalia" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images, from angry protests over a housing crisis that has dominated Spain's election campaign, to Leo XIV's visit to his adopted homeland Peru and "Rocky" fans marking 50 years since the release of boxing movie classic.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French Ciryl Gane retains MMA heavyweaight title agianst Josh Hokit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fad498fc1a811c983c9b56c158ff68b5b63e026b1481c076b542990990df30e</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:58:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-cyril-gane-retains-mma-heavyweaight-title-agianst-josh-hokit--7376b8bda429.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-cyril-gane-retains-mma-heavyweaight-title-agianst-josh-hokit" /><summary type="html">Ciryl Gane remains the world's MMA heavyweight champion. Overnight, the French athlete beat Josh Hokit in the main event of UFC 334 at Madison Square Garden in ​New York. The 5-round fight was rough, as Shirli Sitbon explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bahrain says air defences destroyed several Iranian drones attacking US base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee2701bee2f4ae5a8d47bcd4b93a771446bc95c61dfa9046227b0db8688caef</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:55:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base--e8fd9186a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base" /><summary type="html">Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September. The second Iranian drone attack in three days, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East war. Diplomatic efforts to end the almost nine-month conflict have yet to produce a breakthrough, with ​sporadic attacks continuing. Details from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran, Reza Sayah.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's presidential race heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f445c549751bea92624c68a4487107c6976e2eb1286a997d05cb1bc383e75baa</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:49:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-week-in-france/20261115-france-s-presidential-race-heats-up--2c609c28dc04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-week-in-france/20261115-france-s-presidential-race-heats-up" /><summary type="html">In approximately six months time, French voters will head to the polls for the first round of the presidential election.  Due to term limits, current president Emmanuel Macron is barred from running again. But that hasn't stopped a whole host of candidates from tossing their hat in the ring.</summary><category term="A week in France" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drones strike Russia's petrochemical capital in overnight assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a8e13c3c15f5030ace6a35081c36dba643f312db9d395ed2ef39bc4f2b43c9a</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:36:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-ukrainian-drones-strike-russia-s-petrochemical-capital-in-overnight-assault--7a9e9db839b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-ukrainian-drones-strike-russia-s-petrochemical-capital-in-overnight-assault" /><summary type="html">Russian officials confirmed Sunday that the central industrial city of Nizhnekamsk had endured "prolonged" Ukrainian airstrikes overnight, damaging a residential building and sparking a fire at a major petrochemical complex, injuring three people. Separate overnight strikes on Taganrog city killed an electricity substation engineer, according to the regional governor.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The Philippines and Australia strengthen joint military deterrence at ASEAN summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b45ba93b2065c08dc9b6baf584bc430202fba7075dfdd65ced320cd3847d3484</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:18:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-philippines-and-australia-strengthen-joint-military-deterrence-at-asean-summit--c08df64c21da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-philippines-and-australia-strengthen-joint-military-deterrence-at-asean-summit" /><summary type="html">Southeast Asian leaders opened their annual summit in the Philippine capital Manila on Sunday. During three days, world leaders are expected to focus on trade, energy and conflict – including the war in Iran. Donald Trump is expected to land in Manila on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Bangkok Tommy Walker.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Ukraine make territorial concessions for NATO membership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de7a1423852c12e8fb76f88ca351f4b46e73fda399249ac2fd19f4863e25fe9e</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:14:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/will-ukraine-make-territorial-concessions-for-nato-membership--900152e56ff1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/will-ukraine-make-territorial-concessions-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">The United States suggested Ukraine make territorial concessions in exchange for a NATO membership, according to Volodymyr Zelensky. The Ukrainian president also claims that Russia has rejected an energy truce. This week’s US-mediated negotiations did not result in any tangible progress. Story by Simon Moritz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Air travel issues persist in the US after nationwide ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a8dcb3e7d5b2f49fed4b609f6d2a3fe014b644ab2dc3b9aa447e107499bfc6c</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:12:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop--ae8922ebd6d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop" /><summary type="html">After almost five hours of grounded flights in the US, flights have resumed. However, passengers are still waiting and wading through tough logistics to get to their destinations after massive delays and cancelled flights. Details by Simon Moritz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Francophone summit opens in Cambodia, overshadowed by tensions in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9429a77dcd9da8b9f47021aad7ebd2c96c47649fc01a2f279b4c5512fd3d2214</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:06:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-francophone-summit-opens-in-cambodia-overshadowed-by-tensions-in-africa--3f0236d52bb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-francophone-summit-opens-in-cambodia-overshadowed-by-tensions-in-africa" /><summary type="html">The 20th Francophonie Summit opened on Sunday in Phnom Penh, Cambodia, overshadowed by a high-stakes leadership dispute. The International Organisation of the Francophonie is set to elect its next secretary-general on Monday for a four-year term, but escalating friction between Rwanda, which has led the OIF for eight years, and the Democratic Republic of Congo has thrown the summit into crisis. Details by Liza Kaminov.</summary></entry><entry><title>Illegal mining threatens French Guiana forests and indigenous communities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f72d3a4189804c9121bcd87ade21b69de9b813f8471243ab09c9d5c1e661c82b</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:04:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/illegal-mining-threatens-french-guiana-forests-and-indigenous-communities--6cac6d2cceef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/illegal-mining-threatens-french-guiana-forests-and-indigenous-communities" /><summary type="html">In French Guiana, the fight against illegal gold mining is rapidly being lost and creating an environmental and health disaster, according to the World Wildlife Fund. During an aerial survey in early August, park rangers counted 239 illegal sites within the protected area in record.</summary></entry><entry><title>Are we too reliant on technology? Questions arise after Microsoft's widespread outages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d554f1428d0549a32e01ba18c3c2996278e31f7e5b2f8e7da2e856cbaf6243ff</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T11:44:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/are-we-too-reliant-on-technology-questions-arise-after-microsoft-s-widespread-outages--4b1ea9525098.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/are-we-too-reliant-on-technology-questions-arise-after-microsoft-s-widespread-outages" /><summary type="html">This week's Microsoft outage highlighted the risks of relying on a single technology provider for essential services. The disruption lasted nearly 24 hours, impacting millions of users across more than 70 countries – from government agencies to airlines to hospitals and small businesses. Are we too reliant on technology? Analysis by Marcel Saucet, research associate at the University of San Diego School of Law.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope laments poverty-stricken Inca communities as locals leave Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a90b17813f13de4b5e1ddefd0014299fa6fb7172357d0439e3deae20ce9b136</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:55:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru--5c41da65bfa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Sunday will traverse the length of Peru in what marks the penultimate day of his Latin American tour. The leader of the Catholic church – who underwent cancer surgery just a month ago – warned that Peru's remote Inca communities are under threat as poverty continues to drive locals out of their homeland in search of better futures.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Global diesel prices ease as winter approaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28609d9b41b9987f7a3c64ec00dc20e15f61b29805cefb8ee1594fffe14e8491</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:40:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/global-diesel-prices-ease-as-winter-approaches--8c37061055b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/global-diesel-prices-ease-as-winter-approaches" /><summary type="html">Global diesel prices, which have remained elevated since the start of the Iran war and the blockade of the Strait of Hormuz, have fallen sharply in recent weeks as Gulf exports recover and global oil supplies get back on track for the first time since February. The price drop is being felt in Europe, where prices remain roughly 77% above pre-war levels, and in the US, where the national average fell below $6 a gallon on Saturday. Details by Liza Kaminov.</summary></entry><entry><title>Philippine star Carmelle wins first Asian edition of Eurovision song contest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48f5850e7542eb6709fd01401a602a68ea882a56d50efe741a93eb1876659fe7</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:45:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:26:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/philippine-star-carmelle-wins-first-asian-edition-of-eurovision-song-contest--7050e4e4ce01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/philippine-star-carmelle-wins-first-asian-edition-of-eurovision-song-contest" /><summary type="html">The Philippines has won the first Asian edition of the Eurovision Song Contest. The Filipino singer beat ten other acts to take the title in Bangkok, with a song celebrating women's empowerment. A taste of the winning song with Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran claims attack on US military airbase in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a732a2e7685ce247fe25507b3d0992e7395e62986e8793d288411d3358613f12</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:46:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T09:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-iran-claims-attack-on-us-military-airbase-in-bahrain--23e345aee6b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-iran-claims-attack-on-us-military-airbase-in-bahrain" /><summary type="html">Iranian military confirmed on Sunday an attack on a US military base in Bahrain, in its second targeting the Middle Eastern country in the space of three days. Bahrain's military said it had intercepted several Iranian attacks, with the foreign ministry confirming its air defence systems had shot down Iranian drones, preventing them from reaching their intended targets.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX makes rocketry history by recapturing massive reusable rocketship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6dde3ac0766b891fc699f30b7eb7d0141f6627cdd8d5ea0e4558da29f46fa2a</id><updated>2026-11-15T15:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T09:42:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spacex-makes-rocketry-history-by-recapturing-massive-reusable-rocketship--f03cae991aee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-makes-rocketry-history-by-recapturing-massive-reusable-rocketship" /><summary type="html">After failing to catch a booster yesterday, SpaceX managed to recapture its massive reusable rocketship, "Starship" for the first time. Smaller previous models have successfully relanded but they require heavy legs and aren't fully reusable. Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry></feed>
